# OpenLane run intermediates. The patterns are deliberately the SAME two the
# filter-repo rewrite removed, so the ignore rule and history agree:
#   tmp/                    33.63 MB  Yosys .lib cell dumps
#   05-yosys-jsonheader/     5.96 MB  JSON header dump
# What is kept is 1.16 MB of evidence -- resolved.json, flow.log, error.log,
# warning.log and the .rpt timing reports -- which is where the ECP5/SKY130
# numbers in CLAUDE.md come from. Ignoring the whole runs/ tree instead would
# silently un-track that evidence on the next `git rm -r --cached`.
#
# The original rules were `hdl/openlane/runs/` and `hdl/openlane/mul48/runs/`,
# which missed `hdl/openlane/ldl/runs/` -- the only one that ever existed. So
# 39.6 MB got committed and .gitignore could not stop them: it never matched the
# path. Untracking alone would not have shrunk the push either, since the files
# were in history; that needed the filter-repo rewrite.
hdl/openlane/runs/
hdl/openlane/*/runs/*/tmp/
hdl/openlane/*/runs/*/05-yosys-jsonheader/
*.vcd
*.gtkw

# OS
.DS_Store

# personal notes (not part of the repo)
notes/
session-*.md

# scratch staging for container benches (logs must be reachable from the
# Docker bind mount, which does not see /tmp on WSL2)
.work/
